In this case, it doesn't matter.  However, compiling a program depends on the
size of the compiler and the level of nesting of the program being compiled. 
The program may have it's own memory requirements.

(sample program that takes much more memory to run than compile)

int main(void)
{
   char *s;

   s=(char *)malloc(1024*1024*256*sizeof(char));  /* Allocate 256 Meg memory block */
   printf("%d\n",s[1024*1024*256-1]);     /* Print last char in block */
   free(s);                               /* Return memory */
};

